{title: There Is a Green Hill Far Away}
{artist: Cecil F. Alexander / George C. Stebbins}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 71}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 202)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]There is a green hill [A]far a[D]way,
[D]Out[A]side a city [D]wall,
[D]Where the dear Lord was [A]cruci[Bm]fied,
[Bm]Who died to [E7]save us [A7]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A7]O dearly, dearly, [D]has He loved,
[D]And [Bm]we must love Him, [A]too,
[A]And [D]trust in His re[Bb]deeming blood,
[Bb]And try His works to [D]do.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]We may not know, we [A]cannot [D]tell,
[D]What [A]pains He had to [D]bear;
[D]But we believe it [A]was for [Bm]us
[Bm]He hung and [E7]suffered [A7]there.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]He died that we might [A]be for[D]giv’n,
[D]He [A]died to make us [D]good,
[D]That we might go at [A]last to [Bm]Heav’n,
[Bm]Saved by His [E7]precious [A7]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]O dearly, dearly [A]has He [D]loved,
[D]And [A]we must love Him, [D]too,
[D]And trust in His re[A]deeming [Bm]blood,
[Bm]And try His [E7]works to [A7]do.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
